.TH 0C-MCP 1 "@DATE@" "0c-ime @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
0c-mcp \- connect stdio MCP clients to the 0c Zhuyin input method
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 0c-mcp
.RB [ \-dir
.IR directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 0c-mcp
lets AI assistants that only speak the Model Context Protocol over standard
input and output manage the personal vocabulary of the 0c
(\[u9748]\[u7280]\[u6CE8]\[u97F3]) Zhuyin input method.
It reads JSON-RPC messages line by line from standard input, forwards each one
to the local API at
.I http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp
and writes the responses to standard output.
.PP
The local API is off by default; enable it with
.BR "0c-update api enable" .
The access token is read from the user's data directory for every request,
so the client configuration does not need to contain it and keeps working
after the token is regenerated.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-dir " directory"
The user's data directory that holds
.IR api.json " and " api-token.json .
The default is
.IR ~/.local/share/zuin .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 0c-update (1)
